1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:16,300
The voice you're about to hear reading Lord Byron's 'She Walks in Beauty' isn't me.

2
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:24,008
She walks in beauty, like the night

3
00:00:26,925 --> 00:00:32,091
Of cloudless climes and starry skies

4
00:00:33,008 --> 00:00:38,674
And all that's best of dark and bright

5
00:00:40,049 --> 00:00:47,466
Meet in her aspect and her eyes

6
00:00:47,841 --> 00:00:51,091
Thus mellowed to that tender light

7
00:00:53,174 --> 00:00:56,758
Which heaven to gaudy day denies

8
00:00:56,758 --> 00:00:59,883
One shade the more, one ray the less

9
00:00:59,883 --> 00:01:02,633
Had half impaired the nameless grace

10
00:01:02,633 --> 00:01:05,758
Which waves in every raven tress

11
00:01:05,799 --> 00:01:08,758
Or softly lightens o'er her face

12
00:01:08,758 --> 00:01:11,383
Where thoughts serenely sweet express

13
00:01:11,383 --> 00:01:17,049
How pure, how dear their dwelling-place

14
00:01:17,174 --> 00:01:20,549
And on that cheek, and o'er that brow

15
00:01:20,549 --> 00:01:23,424
So soft, so calm, yet eloquent

16
00:01:23,424 --> 00:01:26,591
The smiles that win, the tints that glow

17
00:01:26,591 --> 00:01:29,383
But tell of days in goodness spent

18
00:01:29,383 --> 00:01:32,258
A mind at peace with all below

19
00:01:35,133 --> 00:01:37,883
A heart whose love is innocent!

20
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:53,643
Lord Byron — 1814 / read by Nate
